00:46:52,067 --> 00:47:17,572
Moving up on top of that, the Eka group comes from the early Permian, as the southern continents shifted northward, and we started to get warmer climates coming out of that glacial period. These deposits in the Karu Basin record an extensive freshwater system of lakes and rivers, fossils in there that we start to see, Glossopteris, the famous plants.

