As I say, I've heard that name before. I wouldn't have been able to tell you much about it, but I knew I had heard it. The Beaufort group covers the rest of the Permian and then into the Triassic. Within the Permian, this section of the Karu supergroup includes tons of very famous fossils, including early reptiles like Yungenia and Eunodosaurus, which is the ancient proposed turtle ancestor.

