00:49:32,512 --> 00:49:37,433
Which is why we call the other one less extreme. Yes, the one that overshadows the first one.

270
00:49:37,766 --> 00:49:57,031
Yep. Sediments within the Karu supergroup, very excitingly, span the whole of both events. They start beforehand, they document the ecosystems that were there before, they document the extinction events, they document the recovery afterwards.

