Because like we've mentioned, so often, mass extinction events, while dramatic and not instantaneous, are very fast events in the geologic record, you know, dealing with maybe just thousands of years. So it's very often that we really only get a look at the before and after picture, which can tell us a lot, but not necessarily how we got from A to B.

273
00:50:34,228 --> 00:50:51,192
And often we don't even have both of those. Yes, exactly. We might have just after or just before. And so getting information during the big extinction event is hugely informative for it, but also like extinction understanding in general.

